UID:camargo-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Camargo Fellowship 2027-2028 for Artists\, Scholars and T
 hinkers (Cassis\, France)
DESCRIPTION:The Camargo Foundation invites artists\, scholars and thinkers 
 to its flagship Core Fellowship: a ten-week self-directed residency on its
  clifftop campus overlooking the Mediterranean in Cassis\, France\, dedica
 ted to research\, experimentation and interdisciplinary exchange. Curators
  apply under the Thinkers category\, which covers accomplished professiona
 ls and practitioners in cultural and creative fields who are professionall
 y engaged in critical thought\, including curators\, critics and journalis
 ts\; projects should engage theoretical\, artistic or societal questions. 
 WHAT YOU GET: a stipend of EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 total)\, basic tra
 nsportation funding\, and a furnished apartment with an equipped kitchen o
 n campus. Fourteen fellowships are awarded per year: seven for artists and
  seven for scholars and thinkers. RESIDENCY PERIODS: Fall 2027 (8 Septembe
 r to 17 November 2027) or Spring 2028 (23 February to 4 May 2028). ELIGIBI
 LITY: artists in visual arts\, performance\, writing\, film\, music or mul
 tidisciplinary work with at least 5 years of professional practice\; schol
 ars holding or pursuing a PhD focused on French and Francophone cultures o
 r cross-cultural Mediterranean studies\; and thinkers as described above. 
 APPLICATION: via Submittable with a 100-word proposal summary\, a 1\,200-w
 ord proposal narrative\, a 300-word rationale for Camargo\, a 300-word car
 eer-stage rationale\, a CV (max 3 pages)\, work samples and two references
 . NOTE: the foundation has announced that this is the final Fellowship sel
 ected through a public open call until further notice\; a new selection pr
 ocess begins in July 2027\, making this the last chance to apply directly.
 \n\nOrganisation: Camargo Foundation\nLocation: Camargo Foundation campus\
 , Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.\nAward: EUR 350 per week (EUR 3\,500 to
 tal for the ten-week residency)\, plus basic travel funding and a furnishe
 d apartment with equipped kitchen on the Camargo campus. 14 fellowships pe
 r year: 7 for artists and 7 for scholars and thinkers. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Ten weeks\, either 8 September to 17 November 2027 or 23 Febru
 ary to 4 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fello
 wship-2026-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://camargofoundation.org/en/camargo-fellowship-2026-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Camargo Foundation campus\, Cassis\, France. Open worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nordic-culture-fund-enter-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Deadline: Nordic Culture Fund: ENTER 2026 (exploratory cross-border
  collaboration)
DESCRIPTION:ENTER is the first programme in the Nordic Culture Fund's new p
 ortfolio\, designed to support ambitious ideas that need collaboration to 
 be explored and tested in practice. It offers space to experiment\, learn 
 as you go and test new directions through encounters across disciplines an
 d perspectives\, rather than funding finished productions. WHO CAN APPLY: 
 individuals\, groups\, organisations\, institutions\, associations and com
 panies\, from arts and culture or other sectors\, as long as arts and cult
 ure are central to the initiative. Initiatives need clear Nordic anchoring
  (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\; applicants and pa
 rtners may be based anywhere\, and multiple applications for different ini
 tiatives are permitted. FUNDING: up to DKK 50\,000\, plus up to DKK 25\,00
 0 in accessibility support\, with no co-funding requirement. WHAT IT DOES 
 NOT SUPPORT: education or study visits\, conference or festival participat
 ion\, tours or travelling exhibitions\, productions or publications\, orga
 nisational running costs\, or construction and equipment purchases. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted electronically through the Fund's portal in Danish\, Norw
 egian\, Swedish\, Finnish or English\; no attachments are allowed\, so eve
 rything must fit in the form. Decisions come within five weeks of the dead
 line. The autumn 2026 window runs 14 September to 16 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Nordic Culture Fund\nLocation: Nordic region and beyond. Initiat
 ives must have clear Nordic anchoring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-bor
 der collaboration\, but applicants and partners may be based anywhere.\nAw
 ard: Up to DKK 50\,000 (roughly EUR 6\,700)\, plus up to DKK 25\,000 in ad
 ditional accessibility support for logistics and access needs\, for a maxi
 mum total of DKK 75\,000. No co-funding required. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Projects may run up to one year from the stated start date\, genera
 lly non-extendable.\n\nMore: https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-prog
 rammes/give-ambitious-ideas-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nordiskkulturfond.org/en/funding-programmes/give-ambitious-idea
 s-space-to-grow-with-enter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Nordic region and beyond. Initiatives must have clear Nordic ancho
 ring (interpreted flexibly) and cross-border collaboration\, but applicant
 s and partners may be based anywhere.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ietm-global-connect-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: IETM Global Connect 2027 (performing arts professionals w
 orldwide)
DESCRIPTION:IETM Global Connect brings up to 10 contemporary performing art
 s professionals from outside the network into IETM\, the international net
 work for contemporary performing arts\, created with and supported by the 
 IETM Associate Members and co-funded by the European Union. WHAT YOU GET: 
 free IETM membership for five years (2027 to 2031) with free access to all
  IETM meetings and training programmes\; online community-building session
 s and peer learning from January to May 2027\; and funded participation in
  the 2027 IETM Plenary Meeting in Larnaka\, Cyprus (25 to 28 May 2027)\, w
 ith travel\, accommodation\, visa and subsistence costs covered based on e
 ach participant's location. ELIGIBILITY: producers\, artists\, managers\, 
 presenters and other contemporary performing arts professionals from anywh
 ere in the world with at least five years of professional experience\; a d
 emonstrated commitment to equality\, inclusion\, diversity and sustainabil
 ity\; proficient English\; and availability to travel to Cyprus in May 202
 7 (Schengen visa support provided if needed). Current IETM members and Glo
 bal Connect alumni cannot apply\; priority goes to professionals from regi
 ons or communities underrepresented in the network. Selection weighs motiv
 ation\, local impact\, innovative practices and career development potenti
 al. DEADLINE: 15 October 2026\, 23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: IETM\, Intern
 ational Network for Contemporary Performing Arts\, with the IETM Associate
  Members\; co-funded by the European Union\nLocation: Online (January to M
 ay 2027) plus the IETM Plenary Meeting in Larnaka\, Cyprus (25 to 28 May 2
 027). Open to contemporary performing arts professionals worldwide\; prior
 ity for professionals from underrepresented regions or communities. Curren
 t IETM members and Global Connect alumni are not eligible.\nAward: Up to 1
 0 places\, each fully supported: free IETM membership for five years (2027
  to 2031) including free access to all IETM meetings and training programm
 es\, plus funded participation in the 2027 Plenary Meeting in Larnaka cove
 ring travel\, accommodation\, visa and subsistence costs (exact support se
 t per participant location). No application fee.\nDuration: Online communi
 ty-building and peer-learning activities January to May 2027\; Plenary Mee
 ting in Larnaka 25 to 28 May 2027\; membership runs 2027 to 2031.\n\nMore:
  https://www.ietm.org/en/projects/ietm-global-connect/apply-to-the-call?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ietm.org/en/projects/ietm-global-connect/apply-to-the-call?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (January to May 2027) plus the IETM Plenary Meeting in Larn
 aka\, Cyprus (25 to 28 May 2027). Open to contemporary performing arts pro
 fessionals worldwide\; priority for professionals from underrepresented re
 gions or communities. Current IETM members and Global Connect alumni are n
 ot eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-biologica-artxscience-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ars Biologica ArtXScience Residency 2027-2028 (Ars Electr
 onica x Ceske Budejovice ECoC 2028)
DESCRIPTION:A fully funded art-science residency from Ars Electronica and C
 eske Budejovice\, European Capital of Culture 2028\, exploring how art and
  science can collaborate on urgent environmental challenges: climate emerg
 ence\, sustainable agriculture\, geoengineering\, permaculture\, water res
 ource management\, and the broader ecological impacts on local communities
 . Selected residents work in direct collaboration with local scientists in
  Ceske Budejovice. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, designers\, creatives and arti
 st collectives with more than 5 years of professional creative practice an
 d documented interdisciplinary work\; experience in community engagement a
 nd science collaborations is essential\; applicants must be 18+\, of any n
 ationality\, and legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. WHAT YOU G
 ET: a EUR 24\,000 package (EUR 6\,000 artist fee\, up to EUR 15\,000 produ
 ction\, up to EUR 3\,000 travel and subsistence) plus one month of housing
  covered separately\; two winners are selected. STRUCTURE: the residency r
 uns January 2027 to April 2028\, with a required on-site stay of up to one
  month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/September 2027\
 , and a March 2028 stay for festival installation\, exhibition and deinsta
 llation. HOW TO APPLY: online form with project title\, a written proposal
  of max 250 words\, a scientific direction statement (max 100 words)\, art
 istic vision (max 100 words)\, community connection plan (max 100 words)\,
  a super short pitch (3 to 30 words)\, 3 to 7 images\, an optional 1-minut
 e video\, a portfolio link and contact information. Two-round selection (o
 nline application then interview)\; winners notified by November 2026. Dea
 dline 28 September 2026 at midnight CET.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electronica 
 and Ceske Budejovice - European Capital of Culture 2028\nLocation: Ceske B
 udejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any nationality aged 18+
  who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Required on-site s
 tays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional stay in August/
 September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibition and deinstal
 lation.\nAward: EUR 24\,000 total package per winner: EUR 6\,000 artist fe
 e\, up to EUR 15\,000 production budget\, and up to EUR 3\,000 for travel\
 , accommodation and subsistence\, plus a separate budget covering one mont
 h of housing in Ceske Budejovice. Two positions available. Free to apply.\
 nDuration: January 2027 to April 2028\, with on-site blocks in early 2027 
 and March 2028\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars
 -biologica-art-science-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/export/en/ecoc2028-ars-biologica-art-scienc
 e-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ceske Budejovice\, Czech Republic. Open to applicants of any natio
 nality aged 18+ who are legally eligible to work and travel in the EU. Req
 uired on-site stays: up to one month in February/March 2027\, an optional 
 stay in August/September 2027\, and March 2028 for installation\, exhibiti
 on and deinstallation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:british-council-connections-through-culture-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:Deadline: Connections Through Culture Grants 2026 (British Council)
DESCRIPTION:Connections Through Culture (CTC) grants are designed to enable
  meaningful partnerships\, cross-cultural exchange and long-term collabora
 tion between the UK and participating countries. In 2026\, CTC incorporate
 s the grants programmes formerly known as Biennials Connect (Visual Arts) 
 and Architecture\, Design and Fashion Biennials and Festivals Grants\, and
  serves as the British Council's major Arts grants programme for 2026 (in 
 place of International Collaboration Grants). It offers grants of between 
 GBP 5\,000 and GBP 15\,000 to support creative practitioners\, cultural pr
 ofessionals\, artists\, organisations\, festivals\, biennials\, hubs and c
 ollectives to develop and deliver collaborative projects across a wide ran
 ge of themes and art forms\, including applied arts\, architecture\, curat
 ing\, dance\, design\, digital\, drawing\, education\, fashion\, film\, in
 stallation\, interdisciplinary work\, painting\, performance\, photography
 \, printmaking\, public art\, research\, sculpture\, social practice\, sou
 nd art\, textiles\, video\, visual arts and writing. ELIGIBILITY: applicat
 ions must involve collaboration between at least one UK-based partner and 
 at least one partner based in an eligible participating country\; each par
 tner must be legally based in the country they are applying from at the ti
 me of application and throughout the project activity period. PARTICIPATIN
 G COUNTRIES: Albania\, Argentina\, Australia\, Bangladesh\, Bosnia and Her
 zegovina\, Colombia\, Mainland China\, Egypt\, Indonesia\, Kazakhstan\, Ke
 nya\, Kosovo\, Lebanon\, Malaysia\, Mexico\, Montenegro\, New Zealand\, Ni
 geria\, North Macedonia\, Pakistan\, Palestine\, Peru\, Philippines\, Saud
 i Arabia\, Serbia\, South Africa\, Tanzania\, Thailand\, Tunisia\, Turkey\
 , United Arab Emirates\, UK\, Ukraine\, Uzbekistan\, Venezuela\, and Vietn
 am. Eligible applicants include artists and creative practitioners\, arts 
 and cultural organisations\, festivals and biennials\, cultural profession
 als\, creative hubs/networks/collectives\, and organisations working acros
 s arts\, culture and the creative sectors. Note: applications involving pr
 ojects organised by or taking place as part of Visual Arts\, Architecture\
 , Design\, Fashion and Craft festivals should be made by the festival or b
 iennial organisation rather than by individual artists\, designers or prac
 titioners. No application fee. Deadline 12 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: B
 ritish Council\nLocation: International collaboration grant. Each applicat
 ion must involve at least one UK-based partner and at least one partner ba
 sed in an eligible participating country\; each partner must be legally ba
 sed in the country they apply from throughout the project.\nAward: Grants 
 of between GBP 5\,000 and GBP 15\,000. Free to apply.\nDuration: Project-b
 ased\; develop and deliver collaborative projects across a range of themes
  and art forms.\n\nMore: https://arts.britishcouncil.org/connections-throu
 gh-culture?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.britishcouncil.org/connections-through-culture?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International collaboration grant. Each application must involve a
 t least one UK-based partner and at least one partner based in an eligible
  participating country\; each partner must be legally based in the country
  they apply from throughout the project.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:social-shifters-global-innovation-challenge-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Social Shifters Global Innovation Challenge 2026
DESCRIPTION:Social Shifters\, a Scottish-registered charity backed by corpo
 rate partners\, runs its Global Innovation Challenge as a funnel into a lo
 nger founder-development pipeline rather than a one-off prize. ELIGIBILITY
 : founders aged 18 to 30 at submission\, leading a fully youth-led venture
  that is already live and producing measurable social or environmental imp
 act\, aligned to at least one Sustainable Development Goal\; concept-stage
  ideas and student projects do not qualify. Multiple winners receive up to
  USD 15\,000 each\, plus pitch coaching\, a finalist showcase\, and ongoin
 g access to fellowships and paid work through the Shifters 100 alumni netw
 ork. Free coaching is available from the moment you register\, so the payo
 ff to registering early is high. Submissions close 31 August 2026 (5pm UTC
 )\, with finalists announced in October and winners in December 2026. Appl
 y at https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Social Shifters\nLocation: Global\; open to youth-led ventures fro
 m anywhere in the world.\nAward: Multiple awards of up to USD 15\,000 each
  (reported grants from USD 3\,000 to USD 15\,000)\, plus pitch coaching\, 
 a finalist showcase\, free founder support from registration\, and ongoing
  access to fellowships and paid work through the Shifters 100 alumni netwo
 rk that corporate partners recruit from. Free to enter.\nDuration: Submiss
 ions close 31 August 2026\; finalists announced October\, winners December
  2026\n\nMore: https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.socialshifters.co/global-innovation-challenge/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global\; open to youth-led ventures from anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ernest-solvay-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: King Baudouin Foundation: Ernest Solvay Fund 2026 (Call f
 or Projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Ernest Solvay Fund provides financial support for local-imp
 act initiatives in three areas: scientific education (science\, technology
 \, engineering and mathematics)\, planet progress (environmental initiativ
 es) and better life (community well-being). ELIGIBILITY: organisations sub
 mitting a project must implement it within a 100 km radius of a Solvay ind
 ustrial\, R&I or administrative site. FUNDING: up to EUR 10\,000 per initi
 ative\; the Fund covers expenses incurred only after the results are annou
 nced (mid-December 2026) and will not reimburse expenses incurred beforeha
 nd. APPLY: create or log in to an account at https://candidate.kbs-frb.be 
 and complete the online application form (it can be saved and completed in
  several stages). Applications are open 15 April 2026 to 30 September 2026
 \; results announced mid-December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Ernest Solv
 ay\, managed with the support of the King Baudouin Foundation\nLocation: O
 rganisations implementing a project within a 100 km radius of a Solvay ind
 ustrial\, R&I or administrative site\nAward: Up to EUR 10\,000 per initiat
 ive. Funding covers only expenses incurred after the results are announced
  (mid-December 2026)\; already-incurred expenses are not reimbursed. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Project implemented after mid-December 2026 anno
 uncement\n\nMore: https://kbs-frb.be/en/2026-ernest-solvay-fund?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kbs-frb.be/en/2026-ernest-solvay-fund?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Organisations implementing a project within a 100 km radius of a S
 olvay industrial\, R&I or administrative site
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count). The inviting foreig
 n party must cover a proportionate share of the costs. Covers hourly fees\
 , travel and accommodation directly related to the activity. IMPORTANT TIM
 ING RULE: applications are accepted from 5 months to a minimum of 7 weeks 
 before the activity begins\, and processing takes about 6 weeks. This lead
  time can rule out activities that fall shortly after a round opens. Round
  2 (4 May to 22 June 2026) has closed. Round 3 runs 8 September 2026 15:00
  CEST to 27 October 2026 16:00 CEST\, with a budget of EUR 33\,000\; given
  the 7-week rule it effectively serves activities starting from late Octob
 er 2026 onwards. IMPORTANT PREREQUISITE: you must already have had an appl
 ication to the Fund positively assessed within the past five years\, and a
  previous voucher does not satisfy this\, so this is not a viable first ap
 proach to the Fund. The window runs 8 September 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 27 Oc
 tober 2026\, but closes early once 20 complete applications are received. 
 Maximum one voucher per applicant per calendar year.\n\nOrganisation: Stim
 uleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation:
  Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within Eur
 ope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per trip
 \n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-voucher
 s?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eu-japan-fest-mobility-support-2026-aug@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: EU-Japan Fest: Mobility Support 2026 (15 August 2026 Cut-
 Off)
DESCRIPTION:The EU-Japan Fest Japan Committee supports individuals and orga
 nisations developing projects between Japan and European Capitals of Cultu
 re (past\, present or future) as well as other Culture Next member cities.
  PURPOSE: support travel for research\, project planning\, and collaborati
 on\, building creative networks aimed at realising Japan-Europe arts and c
 ulture projects. THEMES (for Japan-Europe collaborative projects): Youth E
 mpowerment\; Nature & Green\; Diversity (DEI)\; Social Regeneration. Proje
 cts may include participants from other regions (e.g. Asia) joining a Japa
 n-Europe project. TARGET APPLICANTS: members of European Capital of Cultur
 e teams\; artists and project organisers (including curators\, designers\,
  etc.)\; researchers in culture/arts\; social entrepreneurs. TIMING: appli
 cations must be submitted at least 6 weeks prior to the travel date\; this
  cut-off covers travel in April 2026 - September 2026. DEADLINE: this card
  is for the 15 August 2026 cut-off (other cut-offs each have their own car
 d). APPLY via the Culture Next collaboration page.\n\nOrganisation: EU-Jap
 an Fest Japan Committee (in partnership with Culture Next)\nLocation: Trav
 el between Japan and European Capitals of Culture / Culture Next member ci
 ties\nAward: JPY 50\,000 to JPY 150\,000 per applicant\, depending on appl
 icant and travel category. No application fee.\nDuration: Travel period Ap
 ril 2026 - September 2026 (applications must be submitted at least 6 weeks
  prior to travel)\n\nMore: https://culturenext.eu/fresh-opportunities-and-
 new-steps-in-our-collaboration-with-eu-japan-fest/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturenext.eu/fresh-opportunities-and-new-steps-in-our-collabo
 ration-with-eu-japan-fest/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Travel between Japan and European Capitals of Culture / Culture Ne
 xt member cities
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kometa-fellows-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kometa Fellows 2026: Field Journalism\, Photography\, and
  Writing
DESCRIPTION:Kometa\, a French literary and journalism magazine\, awards fel
 lowships to journalists\, writers\, and photographers documenting reality 
 in contexts of war\, censorship\, or severe social and political tensions.
  Projects must be rooted in direct field experience and focused on contemp
 orary rather than historical events. Projects already under a contractual 
 agreement are ineligible. AMOUNT: €10\,000 per Fellow\, six Fellows sele
 cted. WHAT FELLOWS RECEIVE: one year of funding\; publication of the compl
 eted project (partial or full) in Kometa\; opportunity to contribute to th
 e monthly newsletter\; mentorship through editorial collaboration. 2026 FO
 CUS AREAS: disinformation and narrative wars\; political and social change
 s in the Gulf. DEADLINE: 31 July 2026. APPLY via the Tally form (https://t
 ally.so/r/J9XxMK)\, in French or English (about 30 to 45 minutes). Contact
 : fellows@kometarevue.com.\n\nOrganisation: Kometa (French literary and jo
 urnalism magazine)\nLocation: Remote / field-based (international)\nAward:
  €10\,000 per Fellow\, six Fellows selected. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: One year of funding for field work and research\n\nMore: https://komet
 arevue.com/page/fellows?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://kometarevue.com/page/fellows?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / field-based (international)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:democracy-stories-lab-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222404Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Democracy Stories Lab: Open Call for Visual Storytellers
DESCRIPTION:The Democracy Stories Lab\, an initiative of People Powered (a 
 global hub for participatory democracy) in partnership with the Democracy 
 Narratives Alliance\, invites creators worldwide to submit visual content 
 -- short videos\, illustrations\, or graphics -- that tells a compelling s
 tory about democracy\, voice\, fairness\, belonging\, and community power.
  Content can be original or already published\, as long as it is the appli
 cant's own work and engages with narrative frameworks from the Democracy N
 arratives Alliance's research on 'How to Talk About Democracy.' Tone is op
 en\; serious and comedic approaches are both welcome. SUBMISSIONS: up to t
 wo finished visual content pieces per applicant\, answering the prompt of 
 what the future would look like if people had a real say in the decisions 
 that shape their lives. FORMATS: primarily visual social media content\, i
 ncluding short videos (under 3 minutes\, vertically oriented) and illustra
 tions\; written or audio pieces are accepted if presented in a visual form
 at\, for example as a filmed performance. Each submission should build on 
 one of five narrative types from the DNA research brief 'How to Talk About
  Democracy': outcome-oriented (how democracy shows results)\, intrinsic-va
 lue (why democracy is the best choice)\, collectivist (the importance of d
 iverse voices)\, individual (how democracy is empowering) and process-orie
 nted (showing democratic institutions work)\; a short creative brief gives
  further guidance. AWARDS: 4 winning entries receive USD $1\,000 each\; 5 
 honorable mentions receive USD $500 each\; all winners receive amplificati
 on across People Powered and Democracy Narratives Alliance communications 
 networks and are featured in a global screening event. WHO CAN APPLY: indi
 vidual creators and small teams anywhere in the world\; especially welcome
 s creators who reach audiences outside usual democracy circles\, who come 
 from communities traditionally with less of a say in public discourse\, an
 d who work in civic tech\, advocacy\, community organising\, comedy\, art\
 , illustration\, games\, or lifestyle content. Applications opened 14 July
  2026 and are submitted through the official form on the People Powered De
 mocracy Narratives Alliance page. Submission deadline: 14 September 2026. 
 Winners announced October-November 2026. Note: the initiative was itself v
 oted into existence through People Powered's participatory budgeting proce
 ss (PP Decides).\n\nOrganisation: People Powered and Democracy Narratives 
 Alliance\nLocation: Worldwide\; remote. Global screening event for winners
 .\nAward: USD $1\,000 for each of 4 winners\; USD $500 for each of 5 honor
 able mentions. Plus amplification across People Powered and Democracy Narr
 atives Alliance networks and feature in a global screening event. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: One-time award.\n\nMore: https://www.peoplepowered.
 org/news-content/announcing-the-democracy-stories-lab?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.peoplepowered.org/news-content/announcing-the-democracy-sto
 ries-lab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\; remote. Global screening event for winners.
